{
  "video": {
    "id": "tMr9XH64rtM",
    "title": "Transcription and Translation, excerpt 1 | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tMr9XH64rtM",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 479,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 131,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 7.275,
      "end": 11.84,
      "duration": 4.565,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Now, onward."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 11.84,
      "end": 13.84,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "Transcription."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 13.84,
      "end": 29.68,
      "duration": 15.84,
      "text": "So, we've got DNA, we'll do two, three, probably three by"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 29.68,
      "end": 30.93,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "now, transcription."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 40.05,
      "end": 45.43,
      "duration": 5.38,
      "text": "So we have DNA goes to DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 45.43,
      "end": 52.47,
      "duration": 7.04,
      "text": "DNA makes RNA, RNA makes protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 52.47,
      "end": 55.21,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "This, by the way, gets the name the central dogma of"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 55.21,
      "end": 56.46,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "molecular biology."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 61.697,
      "end": 66.07,
      "duration": 4.373,
      "text": "Due to Francis Crick, and as an aside, Francis actually"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 66.07,
      "end": 67.78,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "never said DNA goes to RNA goes to protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 67.78,
      "end": 70.61,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "What he said was nucleic acids go to protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 70.61,
      "end": 73.18,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "The information flows from nucleic acids to proteins."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 73.18,
      "end": 75.8,
      "duration": 2.62,
      "text": "He never actually said DNA goes to RNA goes to protein,"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 75.8,
      "end": 76.64,
      "duration": 0.84,
      "text": "and that's an important point."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 76.64,
      "end": 79.6,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "And we'll come to it at some point, probably next time."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 79.6,
      "end": 80.85,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "So, transcription."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 82.58,
      "end": 85.22,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "Here's my genome."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 85.22,
      "end": 86.17,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "Here's my double helix."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 86.17,
      "end": 88.05,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "I'm going to stop wrapping around itself, just because"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 88.05,
      "end": 89.53,
      "duration": 1.48,
      "text": "it's tedious."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 89.53,
      "end": 96.15,
      "duration": 6.62,
      "text": "And here's a chunk of DNA that encodes a gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 96.15,
      "end": 99.68,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "Maybe it's a gene that makes our enzyme for arginine"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 99.68,
      "end": 100.58,
      "duration": 0.9,
      "text": "biosynthesis."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 100.58,
      "end": 103.105,
      "duration": 2.525,
      "text": "Remember, we had our arginine genes and all that."
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 103.105,
      "end": 111.09,
      "duration": 7.985,
      "text": "But what happens is it has a starting point, it has a"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 111.09,
      "end": 112.34,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "stopping point."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 120.16,
      "end": 122.48,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "Five prime to three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 127.64,
      "end": 132.52,
      "duration": 4.88,
      "text": "What happens is there is a signal in the DNA that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 132.52,
      "end": 136.97,
      "duration": 4.45,
      "text": "cell knows how to read called a promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 136.97,
      "end": 141.0,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "And under certain circumstances, this promoter"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 141.0,
      "end": 148.91,
      "duration": 7.91,
      "text": "invites an enzyme to sit down, and the enzyme starts copying."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 148.91,
      "end": 151.62,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "Which direction does this enzyme go?"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 151.62,
      "end": 152.96,
      "duration": 1.34,
      "text": "Five prime to three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 152.96,
      "end": 156.04,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "They all go five prime to three prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 156.04,
      "end": 157.29,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "But it makes RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 159.69,
      "end": 161.57,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "Okay?"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 161.57,
      "end": 165.57,
      "duration": 4.0,
      "text": "And then it gets to certain point, and it stops copying."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 165.57,
      "end": 169.6,
      "duration": 4.03,
      "text": "This process of copying is called transcription, because"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 169.6,
      "end": 172.39,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "it's just a direct transcribing."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 172.39,
      "end": 174.28,
      "duration": 1.89,
      "text": "So what's the difference between DNA and RNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 178.8,
      "end": 179.71,
      "duration": 0.91,
      "text": "Two differences."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 179.71,
      "end": 183.31,
      "duration": 3.6,
      "text": "One, this is two prime deoxyribose."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 186.33,
      "end": 189.29,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "This is ribose."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 189.29,
      "end": 192.24,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "It's not two prime deoxy."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 192.24,
      "end": 193.83,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "It's truly ribose."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 193.83,
      "end": 200.24,
      "duration": 6.41,
      "text": "The other difference, where DNA has T, RNA, has U, uracil."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 200.24,
      "end": 203.58,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "The difference, what's the difference between T and U?"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 203.58,
      "end": 205.66,
      "duration": 2.08,
      "text": "The difference is a methyl group."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 205.66,
      "end": 209.02,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "It's a methyl group in an unimportant position for the"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 209.02,
      "end": 210.16,
      "duration": 1.14,
      "text": "base paring."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 210.16,
      "end": 211.59,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "It doesn't matter."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 211.59,
      "end": 212.8,
      "duration": 1.21,
      "text": "It has an extra methyl group."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 212.8,
      "end": 214.53,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "You can look it up in your book."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 214.53,
      "end": 218.31,
      "duration": 3.78,
      "text": "So for all practical purposes, you, in thinking about"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 218.31,
      "end": 221.17,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "polymerization and five prime to three prime, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 221.17,
      "end": 224.51,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "everything, could imagine the DNA and RNA are the same basic"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 224.51,
      "end": 226.84,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "structure, because it's got one little methyl group that"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 226.84,
      "end": 230.66,
      "duration": 3.82,
      "text": "distinguishes T and U. And it's got a hydroxyl on the two"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 230.66,
      "end": 234.84,
      "duration": 4.18,
      "text": "prime position in the carbon, in the sugar, which actually"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 234.84,
      "end": 235.84,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "isn't anything we use."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 235.84,
      "end": 237.41,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "We never use the two prime."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 237.41,
      "end": 240.66,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "So none of what I've told you is affected by t versus u, or"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 240.66,
      "end": 241.96,
      "duration": 1.3,
      "text": "deoxyribose versus ribose."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 241.96,
      "end": 243.61,
      "duration": 1.65,
      "text": "Now, it turns out it does make a difference"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 243.61,
      "end": 244.62,
      "duration": 1.01,
      "text": "in the overall structure."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 244.62,
      "end": 247.785,
      "duration": 3.165,
      "text": "It's harder to base pair with the ribose there as opposed to"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 247.785,
      "end": 250.82,
      "duration": 3.035,
      "text": "the deoxyribose because they stack differently, et cetera."
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 250.82,
      "end": 252.07,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "It makes a difference to the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 252.07,
      "end": 254.71,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "RNA is less stable, all sorts of things."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 254.71,
      "end": 257.339,
      "duration": 2.629,
      "text": "But for your practical purposes, apart from having to"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 257.339,
      "end": 261.29,
      "duration": 3.951,
      "text": "know that it's T versus U, and deoxyribose versus ribose, you"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 261.29,
      "end": 263.72,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "won't see in this course actually see any real strong"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 263.72,
      "end": 266.49,
      "duration": 2.77,
      "text": "reasons why it matters, but it does matter to the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 266.49,
      "end": 267.66,
      "duration": 1.17,
      "text": "All right."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 267.66,
      "end": 273.68,
      "duration": 6.02,
      "text": "So this enzyme comes along, and it copies a segment of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 273.68,
      "end": 276.81,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "DNA, starting at a promoter."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 276.81,
      "end": 278.4,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "It knows which strand it's on."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 278.4,
      "end": 279.5,
      "duration": 1.1,
      "text": "Remember, this is stranded."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 279.5,
      "end": 280.76,
      "duration": 1.26,
      "text": "It's not like it's going back this way."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 280.76,
      "end": 283.13,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "It has a directionality to it."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 283.13,
      "end": 287.02,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "And in reaches what's called a transcriptional stop signal."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 287.02,
      "end": 292.32,
      "duration": 5.3,
      "text": "Transcriptional stop, which is a certain sequence in the DNA,"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 292.32,
      "end": 294.01,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "and it comes to an end."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 294.01,
      "end": 295.49,
      "duration": 1.48,
      "text": "And it makes an RNA transcript,"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 295.49,
      "end": 297.01,
      "duration": 1.52,
      "text": "which then floats away."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 297.01,
      "end": 298.55,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "Which we'll talk next time, gets"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 298.55,
      "end": 302.1,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "translated into a protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 302.1,
      "end": 303.9,
      "duration": 1.8,
      "text": "And how do you think this works?"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 303.9,
      "end": 308.59,
      "duration": 4.69,
      "text": "It takes nucleotides, RNA nucleotides here, with their"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 308.59,
      "end": 312.46,
      "duration": 3.87,
      "text": "triphosphates, and sticks them on, just like we saw with DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 312.46,
      "end": 316.86,
      "duration": 4.4,
      "text": "And it makes a polymer of RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 316.86,
      "end": 322.66,
      "duration": 5.8,
      "text": "And the enzyme is called RNA polymerase, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 322.66,
      "end": 325.11,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "This is all pretty logical stuff."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 325.11,
      "end": 335.45,
      "duration": 10.34,
      "text": "RNA polymerase comes along and does that."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 335.45,
      "end": 338.76,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "So we get RNA polymerase."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 338.76,
      "end": 357.08,
      "duration": 18.32,
      "text": "Now, when I am a cell, and this is my genome, I have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 357.08,
      "end": 359.01,
      "duration": 1.93,
      "text": "gene that goes this way."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 359.01,
      "end": 363.01,
      "duration": 4.0,
      "text": "Here's its promoter, here's its transcriptional stop."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 363.01,
      "end": 367.16,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "I could also have a gene that goes this way."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 367.16,
      "end": 371.41,
      "duration": 4.25,
      "text": "Here's its promoter, here's its transcriptional stop."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 371.41,
      "end": 374.66,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "Directionality could go in either direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 374.66,
      "end": 379.2,
      "duration": 4.54,
      "text": "RNA polymerase comes along, and with the help of friends,"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 379.2,
      "end": 381.9,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "knows where to start."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 381.9,
      "end": 384.17,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "Those friends could be other proteins that are sitting down"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 384.17,
      "end": 387.11,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "there that RNA polymerase likes to associate with."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 387.11,
      "end": 392.34,
      "duration": 5.23,
      "text": "And which strand is being transcribed?"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 392.34,
      "end": 396.46,
      "duration": 4.12,
      "text": "The bottom strand, or the top strand?"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 396.46,
      "end": 397.24,
      "duration": 0.78,
      "text": "Matters."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 397.24,
      "end": 399.66,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "You get a different single stranded RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 399.66,
      "end": 402.85,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "So RNA, when it floats off, is single stranded."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 402.85,
      "end": 412.08,
      "duration": 9.23,
      "text": "This is going to make a single stranded RNA that, five prime"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 412.08,
      "end": 416.26,
      "duration": 4.18,
      "text": "to three prime RNA that is complimentary to, matching to,"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 416.26,
      "end": 417.14,
      "duration": 0.88,
      "text": "the bottom."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 417.14,
      "end": 423.59,
      "duration": 6.45,
      "text": "This guy, however, will make an RNA that is complimentary"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 423.59,
      "end": 424.84,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "to the top."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 428.5,
      "end": 432.17,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "Much of the business of running your cell is figuring"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 432.17,
      "end": 437.24,
      "duration": 5.07,
      "text": "out which genes you should be transcribing into RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 437.24,
      "end": 440.99,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "It turns out your liver is making different transcripts."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 440.99,
      "end": 443.89,
      "duration": 2.9,
      "text": "It's transcribing different segments of your genome than"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 443.89,
      "end": 445.76,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "say, a muscle cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 445.76,
      "end": 447.7,
      "duration": 1.94,
      "text": "Than say, a brain cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 447.7,
      "end": 452.47,
      "duration": 4.77,
      "text": "All of that machinery of figuring out how one genome"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 452.47,
      "end": 455.74,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "gets read out in different ways by RNA polymerase is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 455.74,
      "end": 457.47,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "problem of gene regulation."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 457.47,
      "end": 461.37,
      "duration": 3.9,
      "text": "And we will talk about that in a little while."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 461.37,
      "end": 464.93,
      "duration": 3.56,
      "text": "What we're going to talk about next time is how that RNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 464.93,
      "end": 469.91,
      "duration": 4.98,
      "text": "transcript gets translated into a protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 469.91,
      "end": 471.43,
      "duration": 1.52,
      "text": "And you guys probably, again, all know this."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 471.43,
      "end": 473.37,
      "duration": 1.94,
      "text": "But nonetheless, we'll talk a little bit about it."
    },
    {
